SpaceCurves -- generation of space curves
*****************************************

Description
===========

SpaceCurves is a package dedicated to generation of curves in P3. The 1.0
version of the package generates smooth curves of a given degree and genus, ACM
curves of a given Hilbert function as well as minimal curves in biliaison class
with a given Rao-module.

The method *note smoothDivisors: smoothDivisors, produces a list of *note
Divisor: Divisor, of a given degree on a given surface. The method *note
curve(Divisor): curve, produces a random curve in a given divisor class. For a
given degree, as one varies the input surface from  a smooth quadric, a smooth
cubic and a rational quartic surface with a double line, all obtainable genus
of a smooth curve will occur (save that of a plane curve). The methods to
create the said surfaces are: *note quadricSurface(Ring): quadricSurface,,
*note cubicSurface(Ring): cubicSurface, and *note quarticSurfaceRational(Ring):
quarticSurfaceRational,.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/101[x,y,z,w];                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : X = quadricSurface(R);                                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : Y = cubicSurface(R);                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : Z = quarticSurfaceRational(R);                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : LD = smoothDivisors(4,X) | smoothDivisors(4,Y) | smoothDivisors(4,Z)    |
|                                                                             |
|o5 = {{1, 3}, {2, 2}, {2, 2, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0}, {2, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0}, {3, 1, 1,|
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     1, 1, 1, 0}, {2, 0, 1, 1, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0}, {3, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 0,|
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     0}}                                                                     |
|                                                                             |
|o5 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : LC = apply(LD,D->curve D);                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

 The method *note curve(ZZ,ZZ): curve, generates a random curve with the
specified degree and genus.

+---------------------------------------------+
|i7 : C = curve(5,2);                         |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i8 : degree C, genus C, isPrime C, isSmooth C|
|                                             |
|o8 = (5, 2, true, true)                      |
|                                             |
|o8 : Sequence                                |
+---------------------------------------------+

The postulation character of a curve is defined to be the negative of the third
numerical difference of its Hilbert function, and gives equivalent information
as the Hilbert function. The method function *note positiveChars(ZZ):
positiveChars, generates all possible postulation characters of an ACM curve of
a given degree. The method *note allACMBetti(List): allACMBetti, generates all
Betti tables of ACM curves with a given postulation character. The method
function *note degreeMatrix(BettiTally): degreeMatrix, converts the Betti table
of an ACM curve to its Hilbert-Burch degree matrix. Finally *note
randomDeterminantalIdeal(Ring,Matrix): randomDeterminantalIdeal, generates a
random determinantal ideal in a given ring with specified degree format.
Combining all three methods we can generate ACM curves of any degree d,
exhausting all possibilities of Betti tables.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : G = positiveChars(8);                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i10 : L = G / allACMBetti;                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i11 : netList L                                                              |
|                                                                             |
|      +------------+------------+                                            |
|      |       0 1 2|            |                                            |
|o11 = |total: 1 3 2|            |                                            |
|      |    0: 1 . .|            |                                            |
|      |    1: . 2 1|            |                                            |
|      |    2: . . .|            |                                            |
|      |    3: . . .|            |                                            |
|      |    4: . . .|            |                                            |
|      |    5: . . .|            |                                            |
|      |    6: . 1 1|            |                                            |
|      +------------+------------+                                            |
|      |       0 1 2|            |                                            |
|      |total: 1 3 2|            |                                            |
|      |    0: 1 . .|            |                                            |
|      |    1: . 1 .|            |                                            |
|      |    2: . 1 1|            |                                            |
|      |    3: . . .|            |                                            |
|      |    4: . . .|            |                                            |
|      |    5: . 1 1|            |                                            |
|      +------------+------------+                                            |
|      |       0 1 2|       0 1 2|                                            |
|      |total: 1 2 1|total: 1 3 2|                                            |
|      |    0: 1 . .|    0: 1 . .|                                            |
|      |    1: . 1 .|    1: . 1 .|                                            |
|      |    2: . . .|    2: . . .|                                            |
|      |    3: . 1 .|    3: . 1 1|                                            |
|      |    4: . . 1|    4: . 1 1|                                            |
|      +------------+------------+                                            |
|      |       0 1 2|            |                                            |
|      |total: 1 4 3|            |                                            |
|      |    0: 1 . .|            |                                            |
|      |    1: . . .|            |                                            |
|      |    2: . 3 2|            |                                            |
|      |    3: . . .|            |                                            |
|      |    4: . 1 1|            |                                            |
|      +------------+------------+                                            |
|      |       0 1 2|       0 1 2|                                            |
|      |total: 1 3 2|total: 1 4 3|                                            |
|      |    0: 1 . .|    0: 1 . .|                                            |
|      |    1: . . .|    1: . . .|                                            |
|      |    2: . 2 .|    2: . 2 1|                                            |
|      |    3: . 1 2|    3: . 2 2|                                            |
|      +------------+------------+                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i12 : apply(L, g                                                             |
|          -> apply(g, B -> randomDeterminantalIdeal(ZZ/101[x,y,z,w],         |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|degreeMatrix B)));                                                           |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

The method *note minimalCurve(Module): minimalCurve, produces a minimal curve
in the biliaison class specified by the finite length module. The method *note
minimalCurve(Ideal): minimalCurve, produces a random minimal curve in the
biliaison class of a given curve.

+--------------------------------------------------------+
|i13 : I = monomialCurveIdeal(R,{1,3,4})                 |
|                                                        |
|                         3      2     2    2    3    2  |
|o13 = ideal (y*z - x*w, z  - y*w , x*z  - y w, y  - x z)|
|                                                        |
|o13 : Ideal of R                                        |
+--------------------------------------------------------+
|i14 : M = raoModule(I)                                  |
|                                                        |
|o14 = cokernel {1} | -w z -y x |                        |
|                                                        |
|                             1                          |
|o14 : R-module, quotient of R                           |
+--------------------------------------------------------+
|i15 : J = minimalCurve M;                               |
|                                                        |
|o15 : Ideal of R                                        |
+--------------------------------------------------------+
|i16 : betti res J                                       |
|                                                        |
|             0 1 2 3                                    |
|o16 = total: 1 4 4 1                                    |
|          0: 1 . . .                                    |
|          1: . 4 4 1                                    |
|                                                        |
|o16 : BettiTally                                        |
+--------------------------------------------------------+


