cubicSurface -- creates a cubicSurface
**************************************

Description
===========

This function takes a polynomial ring in 4 variables over a field as the
coordinate ring of P3 and creates a *note CubicSurface: CubicSurface, in this
ring. The equation of the cubic surface is computed from the blowup of 6 points
in P2, listed in the key BlowUpPoints, along with a rational map P2 -> P3 whose
base loci is the 6 given points.

Synopsis
========

  * Usage: 
        X = quadricSurface(R)
  * Inputs:
      * R, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,
  * Outputs:
      * X, an instance of the type *note CubicSurface: CubicSurface,
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : cubicSurface(ZZ/32003[x,y,z,w])                                         |
|                                                                             |
|                            2           2        2         2                 |
|o1 = ideal(2495x*y*z + 4036y z - 5934y*z  - 2495x w - 4289y w - 1194y*z*w +  |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : CubicSurface                                                            |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|      2           2         2          2         3                           |
|10682z w - 8366x*w  + 214y*w  + 4197z*w  - 11134w )                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note quadricSurface: quadricSurface, -- creates a QuadricSurface
  * *note quarticSurfaceRational: quarticSurfaceRational, -- creates a
    QuarticSurfaceRational

Ways to use cubicSurface:
=========================

  * "cubicSurface(Ring)"

