minimalCurveBetti -- computes the Betti diagram of the minimal curve
********************************************************************

Description
===========

A finite length module M determines a unique biliaison class. Curves of minimal
degrees in this class are called minimal curves. Given the ideal of a curve J,
this function returns the Betti tally of any minimal curve of J. Given a finite
length module M, this function returns the Betti tally of any minimal curve in
the biliaison class specified by M.

Synopsis
========

  * Usage: 
        T = minimalCurveBetti(M)
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,
  * Outputs:
      * T, a *note Betti tally: (Macaulay2Doc)BettiTally,
+----------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/101[x,y,z,w];   |
+----------------------------+
|i2 : M = coker vars R;      |
+----------------------------+
|i3 : I = minimalCurveBetti M|
|                            |
|            0 1 2 3         |
|o3 = total: 1 4 4 1         |
|         0: 1 . . .         |
|         1: . 4 4 1         |
|                            |
|o3 : BettiTally             |
+----------------------------+

Synopsis
========

  * Usage: 
        T = minimalCurve(J) 
  * Inputs:
      * J, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, of a pure dimension one
        subscheme
  * Outputs:
      * T, a *note Betti tally: (Macaulay2Doc)BettiTally,, of a minimal curve
        in the biliaison class
+---------------------------------------+
|i4 : R = ZZ/101[x,y,z,w];              |
+---------------------------------------+
|i5 : J = monomialCurveIdeal(R,{1,3,4});|
|                                       |
|o5 : Ideal of R                        |
+---------------------------------------+
|i6 : I = minimalCurveBetti J           |
|                                       |
|            0 1 2 3                    |
|o6 = total: 1 4 4 1                    |
|         0: 1 . . .                    |
|         1: . 4 4 1                    |
|                                       |
|o6 : BettiTally                        |
+---------------------------------------+

