raoModule -- computes the Rao module of a curve
***********************************************

  * Usage: 
        M = raoModule I
  * Inputs:
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, of a pure dimension one
        subscheme
  * Outputs:
      * M, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,

Description
===========

Given I the homogeneous ideal of a pure dimension one subscheme in P^3, the
function computes its Rao module.
+---------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/101[x,y,z,w];              |
+---------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = monomialCurveIdeal(R,{1,3,4});|
|                                       |
|o2 : Ideal of R                        |
+---------------------------------------+
|i3 : M = raoModule I                   |
|                                       |
|o3 = cokernel {1} | -w z -y x |        |
|                                       |
|                            1          |
|o3 : R-module, quotient of R           |
+---------------------------------------+

Ways to use raoModule:
