smoothDivisors -- produces a list of smooth divisors of a given degree on a surface
***********************************************************************************

Description
===========

Produces a List of *note Divisor: Divisor, of a given degree on a given
surface. On the *note CubicSurface: CubicSurface, and the *note
QuarticSurfaceRational: QuarticSurfaceRational, the list is not exhaustive, but
will include a divisor for each possible genus that a smooth curve can obtain.

Synopsis
========

  * Usage: 
        L = smoothDiviors(d,X)
  * Inputs:
      * d, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, degree
      * X, an instance of the type *note QuadricSurface: QuadricSurface,
  * Outputs:
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, of Divisors
+-----------------------------------------+
|i1 : X = quadricSurface(ZZ/101[x,y,z,w]);|
+-----------------------------------------+
|i2 : L = smoothDivisors(5,X)             |
|                                         |
|o2 = {{1, 4}, {2, 3}}                    |
|                                         |
|o2 : List                                |
+-----------------------------------------+

Synopsis
========

  * Usage: 
        L = smoothDiviors(d,X)
  * Inputs:
      * d, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, degree
      * X, an instance of the type *note CubicSurface: CubicSurface,
  * Outputs:
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, of Divisors
+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : X = cubicSurface(ZZ/101[x,y,z,w]);                                   |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : L = smoothDivisors(5,X)                                              |
|                                                                          |
|o4 = {{2, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0}, {3, 1, 1, 1, 1, 0, 0}, {4, 2, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1}}|
|                                                                          |
|o4 : List                                                                 |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Synopsis
========

  * Usage: 
        L = smoothDiviors(d,X)
  * Inputs:
      * d, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, degree
      * X, an instance of the type *note QuarticSurfaceRational:
        QuarticSurfaceRational,
  * Outputs:
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, of Divisors
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : X = quarticSurfaceRational(ZZ/101[x,y,z,w]);                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : L = smoothDivisors(5,X)                                                 |
|                                                                             |
|o6 = {{3, 0, 2, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 0, 0}, {3, 0, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 0}, {4, 1, |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     2, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1}}                                                |
|                                                                             |
|o6 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

